FROM (VALUES
  ('9694e31d-7aa0-42ad-be8b-f9e3441a85b3','East Central IL Archers is a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D club serving Urbana, Illinois, home to the University of Illinois. The ASA affiliation means members shoot a foam-animal course meant to mimic real bowhunting distances and angles, a format that appeals to hunters as much as target archers looking for something more varied than a flat range. Rick Kumler is the listed contact, the person to reach for shoot days or joining. East-central Illinois is farm country with a solid deer-hunting base, so a 3D club here serves a real local need beyond the university crowd. As with most volunteer clubs, access likely runs around scheduled shoot days rather than set public hours. Contact the club directly for current details.'),
  ('687621f9-3ca8-4362-87b9-df765e1cf1b6','East Coast Archery in Salisbury, Massachusetts combines a USA Archery affiliated club with a genuine full-service setup: a pro shop, lessons, a Junior Olympic Archery Development program, and an Adult Archery Program all in one place. That''s an unusually complete package, letting someone walk in without equipment, take a lesson, get outfitted at the pro shop, and eventually move into structured JOAD or adult programming. Salisbury sits right at the New Hampshire border along the Massachusetts coast, giving it a wide catchment area across the Seacoast region. For families or adults in the area looking for one place covering gear, instruction, and ongoing programs, East Coast Archery is worth contacting directly for current pricing and schedules.'),
  ('fcd35ad6-6330-4791-9cf0-74448fc755e5','East End Archery is a USA Archery affiliated club out on the North Fork of Long Island, based in Peconic, New York, running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program for young archers. The North Fork is better known for wineries and farm stands than shooting sports, so a dedicated JOAD club gives local families an option that would otherwise mean a long drive west toward the city or Nassau County. JOAD''s structured levels give kids a clear progression to work through rather than open-ended practice, which tends to appeal to parents new to the sport. No pro shop or additional course type is confirmed here. Families on the North Fork should contact East End Archery directly for enrollment details.'),
  ('da474802-aecc-49ee-85fe-9c2d4d5d5d37','East River Archery is a USA Archery affiliated club in Orlando, Florida with a real program lineup: a Junior Olympic Archery Development track, an Adult Archery Program, lessons, and ten lanes to shoot on. Ten confirmed lanes is a meaningful detail, enough capacity to run group lessons or program sessions alongside individual practice without everyone competing for space. Orlando''s size and steady population growth support a club running youth, adult, and lesson tracks simultaneously, something smaller-market clubs often can''t sustain. For a family relocating to central Florida, or a beginner wanting real instruction rather than a bow rental and a target, East River Archery''s combination of JOAD, adult programming, and lessons is worth a direct call to check current schedules.'),
  ('0dd90df3-935a-4dfd-b89d-0d036911bed8','Easton Center of Excellence is a USA Archery affiliated club, also based in Chula Vista, California, running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program. Sharing a city and part of its name with a nearby commercial range, this is the club side of the operation, structured around USA Archery''s youth and adult curricula rather than open walk-in shooting. That pairing gives Chula Vista families a full track: a child can start in JOAD while a parent works through the adult program at the same facility. Southern San Diego County has a sizable youth sports base, and JOAD''s step-by-step levels appeal to parents wanting real coaching structure. Contact Easton Center of Excellence directly for current enrollment, age requirements, and program schedules.'),
  ('9d673e0d-4598-4ccf-8b74-94ddc828bdc9','Easton Newberry Archery Club in Newberry, Florida is a USA Archery affiliated club running a genuinely complete program list: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, 3D Archery, Field Archery, and lessons for anyone starting from scratch. Covering that many formats under one roof means members can move between disciplines, from target work to hunting-style 3D rounds to the longer measured distances of field archery, without switching clubs. Newberry sits just outside Gainesville, giving it access to a college-town population alongside its own rural surroundings. For a beginner wanting a lesson, a family looking for JOAD, or an experienced archer wanting 3D and field rounds in one place, Easton Newberry Archery Club is worth contacting directly for current schedules.'),
  ('8b01b751-70b6-44a5-a047-ab586c4f6e6e','Eau Pleine Outdoors Club appears in the IBO pro shop directory, connecting this commercial operation in Stratford, Wisconsin to the International Bowhunting Organization''s network of recognized shops. Central Wisconsin has a deep bowhunting tradition, and IBO recognition typically signals a shop that takes bow tuning, arrow work, and 3D competition seriously rather than a general sporting goods counter. As a commercial venue, it likely doesn''t require membership, though specific hours and services beyond the pro shop listing aren''t detailed in the available data. Stratford is a small community in Marathon County, so a recognized pro shop there serves a real need for archers who''d otherwise drive much further. Anyone in central Wisconsin should contact Eau Pleine Outdoors Club directly to confirm current offerings.'),
  ('fb7b48ce-0137-4c1d-b74c-cbd84a8ec297','Echo Valley Archers is a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D club in West Unon, Iowa, confirmed to run an actual 3D course rather than just carrying the ASA affiliation on paper. That course means foam-animal targets set at varying, often unmarked distances, the format built to mirror real bowhunting shots and popular with hunters sharpening skills before deer season. Travis Wymer is the listed contact, the person to reach out to about shoot days or membership. Northeast Iowa is farm and river-bluff country with a strong hunting tradition, and a volunteer 3D club here fits that culture well. As with most volunteer operations, expect scheduled shoot days rather than fixed public hours. Contact Echo Valley Archers directly to confirm access.'),
  ('1aec07a7-0c97-422c-a2f2-e659a06bc7bb','Ed Eliason JOAD is a USA Archery affiliated club in Monroe, Washington, offering both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program under one name. Monroe sits in the Snohomish River valley northeast of Seattle, and having both youth and adult tracks means the club can serve a parent and child at the same location rather than sending them to separate programs. JOAD''s structured belt-style progression gives young archers clear goals to work toward, while the adult program offers a parallel path for grown beginners or returning shooters. No pro shop or additional lesson program is confirmed here. Families in the Monroe area should contact Ed Eliason JOAD directly for enrollment and schedule details.'),
  ('cec51d39-8609-4671-9cf9-b001d5248c82','Edwardsburg Conservation is listed in the IBO pro shop directory and runs a confirmed 3D course, a solid combination for a commercial operation in Edwardsburg, Michigan, along the Indiana border in the state''s southwest corner. Having both an IBO-recognized pro shop and an actual 3D course on-site means archers can get equipment serviced and then walk straight onto foam targets set at hunting-realistic distances in the same visit. Southwest Michigan and the adjacent Indiana line have a strong bowhunting following, and a facility like this serves that crowd directly rather than just target shooters. No lesson program is confirmed here. Archers near the state line should contact Edwardsburg Conservation directly for hours and current pricing.'),
  ('7b67f07f-7754-4c1a-800b-97ae8d866547','Effingham County Sportsman Club is a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club in Effingham, Illinois, a crossroads town along I-70 and I-57 in the southeastern part of the state. The ASA tie points to a foam-animal 3D course, built to simulate real bowhunting shots at varying, often unmarked distances, appealing to hunters as much as competitive target archers. Kevin Gouchenouer is the listed contact, worth reaching out to for shoot schedules or membership information. Southeastern Illinois has a solid farming and hunting base, and a volunteer sportsman''s club here fits that community well, likely running around scheduled shoot days rather than posted public hours. Anyone interested should contact the club directly to find out when the course is active.'),
  ('4ec431ab-468b-47c2-8f88-7d23123a9faa','El Dorado Hills Bowmen, based in the Sacramento-area foothills community of El Dorado Hills, California, is a USA Archery affiliated club that runs a full slate of programs: Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) for young archers, an Adult Archery Program, 3D Archery, and Field Archery. That range of formats makes it a hybrid operation rather than a single-discipline club, with an on-site 3D course and field course giving members somewhere to actually shoot both styles rather than just talk about them. Lessons are offered too, so newcomers aren''t left to figure out form on their own. It''s a solid option for Northern California archers wanting variety under one roof, though contacting the club directly is the way to confirm current schedules and membership.'),
  ('ddc2c43c-f8e1-428f-9eae-520acaf4f885','Despite the polished name, Elite Archery Academy in Detroit, Michigan is registered as a USA Archery affiliated club, running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program for kids and an Adult Archery Program for grown-up beginners and returning shooters. Lessons are part of the offering, which fits an academy framing aimed at people learning the sport rather than experienced archers looking for a raw lane rental. Detroit doesn''t have an overwhelming number of dedicated archery clubs, so a JOAD-plus-adult setup here fills a real gap for families wanting both youth and grown-up instruction in one place. Specifics on cost and schedule aren''t posted, so reaching out directly is the way to get enrolled.'),
  ('f7ed1466-9014-4b66-936e-18dcb346e93f','In the small central-Kansas town of Ellinwood, the Ellinwood Archery Club runs as an ASA-affiliated 3D archery outfit, putting it in the same competitive circuit that many rural bowhunting clubs across the state use for scored shoots on realistic animal targets. Damian Knop is listed as the contact, a practical starting point for anyone wanting to know about shoot dates, course conditions, or joining as a member. Small-town Kansas clubs like this one tend to be tight-knit and word-of-mouth rather than heavily advertised, so showing up unannounced isn''t the best plan. No other amenities, lanes, or lesson programs are noted, so reaching out to Damian first is the smart move before making the trip.'),
  ('35eaaa78-fdba-47c5-bd04-183372ec42f9','Elmore Archery Club, based in Wetumpka, Alabama, is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club, part of the same competitive circuit that draws bowhunting-minded archers across the state toward realistic animal-target shoots rather than pure paper targets. Ryan Pfeifer is the listed contact, worth reaching out to for shoot schedules, course access, or membership questions since the club doesn''t appear to post much publicly beyond that. Wetumpka sits just north of Montgomery, an area with a solid hunting tradition, and a club like this often functions as a low-key community gathering point more than a storefront business. No lanes, pro shop, or lesson details are noted, so contacting Ryan directly is the surest way to get accurate, current information.'),
  ('7d4f2f45-a6c3-4e7c-a394-b963664b362f','Enduring Freedom Co., also in San Antonio, Texas, is a separate USA Archery affiliated club running a notably full program lineup: Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) for kids, an Adult Archery Program, plus 3D Archery and Field Archery programming for members who want to shoot beyond a straight target range. That breadth makes it a hybrid club serving several kinds of archers under one roof rather than specializing in just one discipline. San Antonio''s size supports more than one serious archery organization, and a club with JOAD alongside 3D and field programs stands out for variety. No lane counts, pro shop, or specific schedules are listed, so contacting the club directly is the way to get current program details.'),
  ('e3601f24-fbb9-41df-b48d-c27198358670','Eros Archery, in the small Connecticut town of Thomaston, pairs USA Archery affiliation with an actual pro shop and lessons on-site, running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program and an Adult Archery Program. That mix of retail, instruction, and youth-and-adult programming makes it a genuinely full-service hybrid operation rather than just a club that meets to shoot. Thomaston sits in Litchfield County, an area with a fair amount of outdoor recreation culture, and a shop with lessons attached is a natural draw for families wanting to get kids into JOAD or adults picking up the sport later in life. Specific lane counts and pricing aren''t listed, so reaching out directly is the way to enroll or shop.'),
  ('c4f655a2-01dc-4706-90b2-583cd3257af3','Etowah County Bowhunters Club, based in Hokes Bluff, Alabama, runs as an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club, the kind of setup built around scored shoots on realistic animal targets rather than a standard paper-target range. Patrick Gray is the club''s listed contact, the person to reach out to for shoot schedules, course conditions, or how to get involved as a member. Northeast Alabama has a strong bowhunting presence, and a county-named club like this typically functions as a community hub for local hunters looking to sharpen their shot before season or compete casually against neighbors. No pro shop, lanes, or lesson programs are listed publicly, so contacting Patrick directly is the reliable way to get current information.'),
  ('ab0fd3fd-da93-40bb-a067-867e792ccfee','Eureka Archery Club sits in Eureka, a small town in south-central Kansas, and operates as an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club, meaning members shoot scored rounds on realistic animal targets as part of a wider bowhunting-oriented circuit. Frank Ray is listed as the contact for the club, a good first call for anyone wanting to know about shoot dates, membership, or the state of the course itself. Rural Kansas clubs like this one tend to run informally, organized by volunteers rather than paid staff, so information beyond word of mouth can be thin. No lanes, pro shop, or lesson details are noted for this listing, which makes reaching Frank directly the most reliable way to get accurate answers.'),
  ('91b01728-b065-4fe4-a522-9646b7f498a9','Evans Joad, located in Angola, New York along the Lake Erie shoreline south of Buffalo, is a USA Archery affiliated club built specifically around a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program, as the name itself signals. That focus makes it squarely a youth-development operation rather than a general-purpose range serving every kind of archer, a useful distinction for parents specifically looking to get kids into Olympic-style recurve or compound coaching. Western New York has pockets of organized archery activity, and a dedicated JOAD club fills a specific niche there. No mention of an adult program, pro shop, or lesson structure beyond JOAD itself is listed, so contacting the club directly is the way to find out about age requirements and enrollment.'),
  ('95d4ddab-508b-477d-872b-a26c8f65767c','Every Arrow Counts Archery, in Madison, Georgia, a small historic town between Atlanta and Augusta, is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program and an Adult Archery Program. Having both age tracks under one roof means families can get kids into structured JOAD coaching while parents pick up the sport themselves at the same club, which isn''t a given for smaller-town operations. Middle Georgia doesn''t have an overwhelming number of dedicated archery clubs, so a dual-program setup here is a genuine resource for the area. No details on lanes, a pro shop, or specific meeting times are listed publicly, so contacting the club directly is the way to get enrolled.'),
  ('b441de84-4eb6-4b58-b40a-06ae917cf5e8','Falcon Archers Joad, based in Canonsburg in southwestern Pennsylvania just south of Pittsburgh, is a USA Archery affiliated club built around a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program, which the club''s own name makes clear is its focus. That youth-development orientation makes it a good fit for parents in the Pittsburgh suburbs specifically looking for structured Olympic-style coaching for kids rather than a general club serving every type of archer. No adult program, pro shop, or lesson structure beyond JOAD itself is mentioned, so its scope looks narrower and more specialized than a typical hybrid club. Anyone interested in enrolling a young archer should contact Falcon Archers directly to ask about age requirements, cost, and practice schedule.'),
  ('202a3e76-06d8-47be-86c6-079a93e89fc2','Fall Creek Valley Conservation Club, in the small community of Markleville, Indiana, is listed as an ASA-affiliated archery club, though its status is noted as expired for 2025, meaning that affiliation may no longer be current. Conservation clubs like this one typically run archery as one of several outdoor activities alongside hunting and land stewardship, rather than as a dedicated standalone range, which is common across rural Indiana. Given the expired status on record, anyone interested in shooting there should confirm directly with the club whether its ASA membership and any related programming have since been renewed before assuming current affiliation. No lanes, pro shop, or lesson details are listed, so a direct call is the only reliable way to get current information.'),
  ('c0c7620f-56bb-4b16-9b60-6efb4bbaaf00','Farmington Fish & Game Club, based in New Durham, New Hampshire, is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club with an actual 3D course on the property, so members aren''t just organized around the discipline on paper, there''s real terrain to shoot it on. Brian Fuller is listed as the contact, worth reaching out to for shoot schedules, course conditions, or how to join. New Hampshire''s Lakes Region has a steady bowhunting presence, and a fish and game club with a working 3D course gives local hunters a realistic way to practice before season. No pro shop or lesson program is noted, so contacting Brian directly is the most reliable way to get current, accurate details about the club.'),
  ('7675e319-04c3-4d80-b075-bb72daa4bbfa','Fat Shafts Archery, in the Bay Area city of Benicia, California, runs a pro shop and lessons alongside its USA Archery affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) and Adult Archery programs, making it a fairly complete operation for archers of any age or experience level. That mix, retail, instruction, and structured youth-and-adult programming, is a strong setup for a suburban Bay Area location where demand likely spans total beginners to competitive JOAD kids. Benicia sits along the Carquinez Strait northeast of San Francisco, giving it a built-in draw from several nearby communities. Specific lane counts and program costs aren''t listed publicly, so contacting the shop directly is the way to enroll in lessons or confirm current offerings.'),
  ('e1a11327-645c-4a10-9245-8f49e6f73353','FC Bowhunters Association, based in Flora Vista in northwestern New Mexico''s San Juan County, runs as an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club oriented toward the same realistic animal-target shooting that bowhunters across the region use to stay sharp between seasons. David Archuleta is the listed contact, a good starting point for questions about shoot dates, course conditions, or membership. Northwestern New Mexico''s high-desert terrain supports a real bowhunting culture, and a club named explicitly around bowhunters signals a group focused more on practical hunting preparation than target-only archery. No pro shop, lanes, or lesson program are listed, so reaching David directly is the most reliable way to get current information before visiting.'),
  ('81c6d5f0-8e5b-4e88-8769-0a4f32f8dc7f','Feraris Archery, located in the small Kentucky community of Manitou, is listed in the International Bowhunting Organization''s pro shop directory, which places it within the network of shops IBO-affiliated 3D shooters and bowhunters commonly rely on for gear and setup work. That IBO listing is a meaningful signal even without much else on record, since IBO pro shops tend to specialize in bowhunting equipment and 3D tuning rather than general sporting goods. Rural Kentucky has a strong bowhunting tradition, and a shop with this kind of affiliation likely serves a dedicated local customer base built on word of mouth. No details on lanes, courses, or lesson availability are listed, so contacting the shop directly is the way to confirm current services.'),
  ('a2402b99-5da9-45b8-9a59-31ed0c32a17f','Fertigs Archery Club, despite the club-sounding name, is classified as a commercial operation in Oil City, in the oil-country region of northwestern Pennsylvania, and it appears in the International Bowhunting Organization''s pro shop directory. That IBO listing suggests it caters to 3D shooters and bowhunters looking for tuning and equipment rather than functioning as a membership-based club in the usual sense. Northwestern Pennsylvania has deep hunting roots, and a pro shop with IBO ties likely draws customers from across several rural counties rather than just Oil City itself. No specifics on lanes, courses, or lesson programs are listed publicly, so anyone wanting service or gear should contact the shop directly to confirm hours and offerings.'),
  ('f81663b6-ba8f-4fa8-ab90-7df4fd20fa29','FFX Archery, in Centreville, Virginia within the Washington DC suburbs of Fairfax County, is a USA Archery affiliated club offering both a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program and an Adult Archery Program, with lessons built into its offerings for people at any starting point. That combination makes it approachable for families wanting to get kids into structured JOAD coaching while adults pick up the sport at the same time. Fairfax County''s dense suburban population supports plenty of demand for organized youth and adult archery instruction, more than a lot of smaller markets could sustain. No lane counts, pro shop, or specific schedule details are listed publicly, so contacting the club directly is the way to enroll.'),
  ('9979eece-08c2-4c61-988c-3a1f134ddfc6','Five Birds Archery, based in Laguna Woods in Orange County, California, is a USA Archery affiliated club running a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program, an Adult Archery Program, and Field Archery, giving it a broader spread of formats than a typical single-focus club. That range covers structured youth coaching, adult participation, and the terrain-and-distance discipline of field archery all under one name, a fairly complete offering for a hybrid operation. Laguna Woods is known as a retirement community, making the presence of both JOAD and adult programming notable for reaching multiple generations in the surrounding Orange County area. No lane counts, pro shop, or specific lesson pricing are listed, so contacting the club directly is the way to get enrolled.'),
  ('076e9be0-bca7-4641-bc34-47dc3718a471','Tucked into the hill country around Winchester, Tennessee, Five or Better Archery operates as a volunteer-run club affiliated with the ASA circuit, putting it on the map for archers chasing 3D competition and casual weekend practice alike. Volunteer clubs like this one tend to run lean, with members pitching in on course upkeep and event days rather than paid staff, so hours and walk-in access can vary by season and shoot schedule. If you''re new to the area or new to ASA-style shooting, reaching out ahead of a visit is the smart move, since volunteer boards are usually happy to point newcomers toward the next scheduled shoot or work day.'),
  ('d9c94700-4925-4051-abba-23fc06d1d39e','Flat Shootin Archery in Tollesboro is one of the volunteer-run clubs that keeps Kentucky''s ASA 3D archery scene alive outside the bigger cities, hosting foam-target courses for members training toward regional and state shoots. Volunteer clubs in this network typically post their shoot calendar rather than keeping storefront hours, so the course opens around scheduled events and work days more than a fixed weekly schedule. For a bowhunter or 3D competitor in the Tollesboro area, this is the kind of low-key club where reputation and word of mouth matter more than marketing. Reach out to the club directly to find the next shoot date or ask about joining.'),
  ('38a848aa-06c4-4aa8-852b-88ac682a8e07','Spring Branch sits in the Texas Hill Country, and Fletcha Brothers Archery Club is part of the ASA-affiliated network of volunteer clubs that keeps 3D archery active across that region. Run by members rather than paid staff, clubs like this typically schedule shoots and work days around the calendar rather than keeping fixed hours, so a course that''s open one weekend may be closed the next. For Hill Country bowhunters looking to sharpen range estimation before deer season, ASA clubs are a natural fit, though specifics on this particular course''s layout aren''t published. Contact the club ahead of a visit to confirm what''s currently running.'),
  ('56e83152-ea3f-4f67-81c4-e522d04e7d28','Flint River Archery Club in Burlington runs as a USA Archery affiliated club, which puts it in the Junior Olympic Archery Development pipeline, the same JOAD structure that feeds young archers toward regional, and eventually Olympic-track, competition. Alongside JOAD, the club also runs 3D archery and offers lessons, giving it a rare split identity between structured youth Olympic-style coaching and the more freeform 3D bowhunting-adjacent format. For a family in southeast Iowa looking to get a kid started in target archery, or an adult wanting instruction, this is a stronger-than-average find. Reach out to the club for JOAD enrollment windows, 3D course access, and lesson availability.'),
  ('089c288b-aa2b-409c-b126-c1042eccf247','Flying Arrows JOAD, based in Washington Township, Ohio, wears its focus in the name: it''s a USA Archery affiliated club built around Junior Olympic Archery Development, the youth pathway that trains kids in Olympic recurve and compound form from beginner level up toward regional competition. The club pairs that with an Adult Archery Program, so it''s not purely a youth operation, giving parents a place to shoot alongside their kids rather than just dropping them off. For families in the Dayton-area suburbs looking for structured, coached archery rather than an open range, this is a solid lead. Contact the club for current JOAD session dates and adult program details.'),
  ('8b34c621-2efe-4a1f-b48c-96ef9924a3ec','Foothills Archery sits in Newton, in North Carolina''s foothills region west of Charlotte, an area with a strong home-grown archery and bowhunting culture. As a club rather than a retail operation, it likely runs on membership and volunteer range days more than fixed public hours, and specifics on its course layout aren''t published here. The foothills terrain around Newton is popular with bowhunters scouting for deer season, and clubs in the area often serve as informal meeting points for exactly that crowd. Anyone interested in shooting here, whether for practice or to connect with local hunters, should contact the club directly to confirm current status and how to get involved.'),
  ('7fb59553-47a9-4b98-beb0-fdf079e7a0be','Foothills Public Shooting Complex in Cherryville runs a 3D archery course as part of the ASA-affiliated volunteer club network spread across North Carolina''s foothills, giving local bowhunters a realistic target course to dial in yardage estimation before deer season. Despite the "public" in the name, it operates with volunteer oversight rather than paid staff, so access typically follows a posted shoot schedule instead of daily open hours. That''s standard for ASA clubs in this part of the state, where the course itself is the draw and the calendar of 3D shoots is what really matters to members. Contact the club for the current 3D shoot schedule and any guest-shooting policy.'),
  ('dd40a801-2aa0-43c9-9a76-04bf0b227127','Form First Archery, based in Bismarck, is about as complete a program as a North Dakota archer could ask for: a USA Archery affiliated club running Junior Olympic Archery Development for kids, an Adult Archery Program, plus both 3D and field archery for members who want to shoot at game-shaped foam or graduated field targets rather than a straight paper line. That range of formats under one club, Olympic-style coaching alongside 3D and field, is unusual and suggests a genuinely active membership base in the Bismarck area. Whether the goal is competitive form work or bowhunting-style practice, Form First covers both. Contact the club for current JOAD, adult, and course-access details.'),
  ('e7955670-1a54-46e6-86ee-98dc61b41699','Fort Caroline Archery Club, named for the nearby historic Fort Caroline site in Jacksonville, runs a 3D course as part of the ASA-affiliated volunteer club circuit and backs it up with an on-site pro shop and lessons, a fuller lineup than most volunteer clubs manage. Having equipment and tuning available on-site alongside instruction means a newcomer doesn''t need to already own a properly set-up bow to start shooting here, which lowers the bar compared to a course-only club. For Jacksonville-area bowhunters and 3D shooters, the combination of course, shop, and coaching in one place is worth the drive. Contact the club for lesson scheduling and current shoot dates.'),
  ('1371efa7-8e90-4017-b1a9-69b4449afee0','Fort Edwards Archery Club, in the eastern West Virginia town of Capon Bridge, is a USA Archery affiliated club running both Junior Olympic Archery Development for younger shooters and an Adult Archery Program for grown members, a structured setup that''s less common in this rural stretch of the state than a plain bowhunting club. The dual JOAD and adult programming means a family could realistically join together rather than one parent just dropping kids off. For eastern panhandle residents looking for coached, Olympic-style instruction rather than an unstructured range, this is a solid option. Contact the club for current JOAD and adult program schedules.'),
  ('1c249378-d2b4-4a92-accc-e5942a6c93bb','Fredericksburg 3d Archery runs its 3D course out of Johnson City, in the heart of Texas Hill Country wine and hunting country, as part of the ASA-affiliated volunteer club network that keeps 3D shooting active across the region. The name signals its focus clearly: this is a foam-target course built for bowhunters dialing in range estimation and shot angles ahead of Hill Country deer season, not a flat indoor lane setup. Being volunteer-run, the course typically opens around a posted shoot schedule rather than daily hours, so timing a visit around an event is the way most members access it. Contact the club for the current 3D shoot calendar and guest policy.'),
  ('a12b5e3a-5f2a-4ab5-bf31-e5d40311a9e2','Freedom Arrowsports LLC operates as a volunteer-run ASA-affiliated club out of Clarksburg, Pennsylvania, part of the statewide 3D archery network that gives bowhunters a place to practice on realistic target setups ahead of Pennsylvania''s archery deer season. The LLC in the name suggests a slightly more formal structure than a purely informal club, though it still runs on the volunteer-club model rather than commercial retail hours. Specific details on the course layout and lane count aren''t published here, which is typical for smaller ASA-affiliated operations in rural Pennsylvania. Archers in the Clarksburg area interested in 3D shooting should contact the club directly for the current shoot schedule.'),
