  ('c8e3345b-dd7e-4fc1-a295-2defadc34d95','Highline Archery, based in Sulphur Rock, a small community in north-central Arkansas, was previously registered as an ASA-affiliated archery club, though the listed status shows the affiliation expired in 2025. That doesn''t necessarily mean the club stopped operating, ASA affiliations lapse for all kinds of administrative reasons, but anyone relying on that connection for competition eligibility should confirm current status first. North-central Arkansas has a solid hunting tradition, and clubs in small towns like Sulphur Rock often continue as informal gathering points even without an active national affiliation. No further detail on hours, dues, or current programming is available here, so contacting the club directly is the only way to get an accurate picture.'),
  ('e7b1e15e-33b9-443a-ad08-92691205137c','Hill Country Bowhunters Association, based in Liberty Hill northwest of Austin, is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club that maintains its own 3D course. Having an actual range on-site, not just an affiliation, gives members a place to shoot lifelike animal targets and sharpen their form ahead of deer season, a serious draw in a region known for whitetail hunting. Central Texas''s Hill Country has a strong bowhunting community, and a club combining ASA ties with a real course tends to attract a more competition-minded membership. Paul Kimbol is the listed contact for questions about shoot dates or joining. Further scheduling details aren''t public, so reaching out directly is the way to learn more.'),
  ('6ac93918-5c89-42fb-8fce-3f845df63995','Hillsdale County Conservation Club, listed under Asseo, Michigan, appears in the IBO pro shop directory despite a name suggesting a member-run conservation group rather than a retail business. Southern Michigan has a strong rural hunting culture, and an IBO connection typically points to ties with 3D archery competition and bowhunting circles rather than pure target shooting. The club''s name points toward Hillsdale County, though the listed city of Asseo doesn''t confirm that connection outright. That mismatch makes it worth confirming directly what kind of access this location offers, whether public range time, a retail counter, or something tied to private membership. No further hours or program details are published beyond the directory entry itself.'),
  ('2ba6828d-36c4-4bbb-a6bf-ee92726e5908','For archers around Manchester, a small city in the mountains of southeastern Kentucky, Hilltop Archery serves as the local ASA-affiliated volunteer club built around 3D archery and bowhunting. Kentucky''s Appalachian foothills carry a long hunting tradition, and clubs tied into ASA competition give local archers a way to practice on realistic targets and stay involved in organized shoots throughout the year. Stanley Simpson is listed as the contact for Hilltop Archery, the person to reach for questions about membership, shoot schedules, or current course conditions. As is typical for volunteer-run clubs in small towns like Manchester, day-to-day details beyond that contact point aren''t published anywhere public, so a direct call is the most reliable way to get current information.'),
  ('e92747d4-507d-447d-9610-cf069054d19a','Hilltop Plantation LLC, despite its business-style name, is registered as an ASA-affiliated volunteer club based in Kiln, a small community in southern Mississippi not far from the Gulf Coast. South Mississippi''s mix of pine forest and coastal plain supports a steady bowhunting culture, and an ASA tie situates this club within a 3D archery competition network that many hunters in the region use to stay sharp through the off-season. Trever Serpas is the listed contact, the right person to reach for questions on shoot dates, course access, or how to get involved. Beyond that contact information, specific hours, dues, and day-to-day operations aren''t published, so reaching out directly is the way to learn more.'),
  ('751547ed-dfc8-4c0f-affb-e138a834c709','Hit List Archery, based in Grants, a small city in west-central New Mexico along historic Route 66, is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club serving the area''s bowhunting community. This part of New Mexico sits near national forest land that draws hunters for elk and deer season, and an ASA-affiliated club here likely gives local archers a structured way to shoot 3D targets and prep before those seasons open. Cody Wood is listed as the club''s contact, a good first call for anyone with questions about membership, shoot dates, or course conditions. As with most volunteer clubs, detailed public information about hours or dues isn''t posted beyond that contact point, so a direct inquiry is the way to get current details.'),
  ('d028bb57-6743-477e-a48b-6810a3efe811','HKC Archery, based in Buford, a city in the fast-growing Gwinnett County suburbs northeast of Atlanta, is a USA Archery affiliated club running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program. JOAD clubs follow a structured, Olympic-style recurve curriculum built to develop younger archers'' fundamentals, often with an eye toward regional and national competition as they progress. Metro Atlanta''s northern suburbs have a solid concentration of youth archery programs, and HKC''s JOAD affiliation places it within that broader development pipeline rather than functioning as a casual shooting group. Specific practice schedules, age ranges, and program costs aren''t listed publicly, so parents or prospective members should contact the club directly for current details before signing up.'),
  ('e2452809-2399-4faa-9e21-d2aadaa28982','Named directly for the North Texas town where it''s based, Holliday Creek Archery Assoc is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club serving the area''s bowhunting and 3D archery community. North Texas has a substantial whitetail hunting population, and an ASA-affiliated group in a town this size likely functions as a central gathering point for local archers rather than one of several nearby options. Alice Keene-Mason is listed as the association''s contact, the right person to reach with questions about shoot dates, membership, or course conditions. Beyond that contact detail, day-to-day operations, dues, and scheduling aren''t published publicly, so reaching out directly remains the most reliable way to learn what the club currently offers.'),
  ('fd355216-b140-4a50-b4ff-77e5c8c4a400','Hollywood Archery, despite the name, is based in Union, a small town in rural southeastern West Virginia rather than anywhere near its namesake in California. It appears in the IBO pro shop directory, tying it to the International Bowhunting Organization''s 3D competition circuit that has a real following in West Virginia''s mountain counties, where bowhunting is deeply embedded in local outdoor life. Beyond that directory listing, no additional public detail exists on hours, inventory, or services offered at this location. Given how little is confirmed beyond the IBO connection, the most reliable way to find out what Hollywood Archery actually provides, whether that''s retail, tuning, or range access, is to contact them directly rather than guess from the name.'),
  ('8421f4f9-7086-45d3-8298-bfe5c219dc63','Home On The Range Archery, in Victoria on the Texas Gulf Coastal Plain, is a USA Archery affiliated club with a lineup covering Junior Olympic Archery Development, an adult archery program, and 3D archery, plus lessons offered directly through the club. That combination means Home On The Range can bring in complete beginners through structured instruction while supporting competitive youth archers through JOAD and adult members interested in 3D shooting, a broad reach for one club. Victoria doesn''t have an overwhelming number of archery options, so a club covering this much ground likely serves as the default choice for many local archers. Specific schedules and costs aren''t published, so contacting the club directly is the way to learn more.'),
  ('d557ee7c-3c7b-4470-b58b-e458df079c8e','Hoot & Holler Archery Academy, in Bossier City across the Red River from Shreveport, is a USA Archery affiliated club that pairs a Junior Olympic Archery Development program with an on-site pro shop and lessons. That combination covers a lot of ground for one academy: structured youth competition training through JOAD, gear available without a separate trip elsewhere, and instruction for archers of any age who want coaching. Shreveport-Bossier''s archery scene benefits from having a facility this well-rounded rather than needing to piece services together across multiple businesses. Specific pricing, class schedules, and what the pro shop stocks aren''t detailed publicly, so contacting the academy directly is the way to plan a visit or enroll.'),
  ('14fda82b-6b59-4ac6-a498-2763ea6003c0','Hooterville Acres Archery, based in Union, a small city in east-central Missouri along the Bourbeuse River, is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club catering to the region''s bowhunting and 3D archery community. This part of Missouri sits within easy reach of the St. Louis metro area but retains a genuinely rural, hunting-oriented character, and an ASA affiliation here signals a club built around scored 3D rounds rather than casual paper-target shooting. Blake Dewert is listed as the club''s contact for questions on shoot dates, membership, or course access. As with most clubs of this type, detailed information on hours and dues isn''t published beyond that contact point, so a direct call remains the most reliable way to get current details.'),
  ('95381e02-8bfc-4a41-a135-252efee3b62c','Hoover Parks and Recreation, serving the Birmingham suburb of Hoover, Alabama, runs a USA Archery affiliated program covering both Junior Olympic Archery Development for younger archers and an adult archery program for grown members of the community. Being run through a municipal parks department rather than a private club generally means more structured public access, built around scheduled classes and seasons rather than informal member shoots. Offering both a youth competitive pathway and an adult track gives Hoover residents of any age a way into the sport through the same program. Specific class schedules, registration details, and costs aren''t listed here, so checking with Hoover Parks and Recreation directly is the way to sign up.'),
  ('be38ab2f-3b9a-4f72-a549-f460521e62ff','Hot Spring County Bowhunters, based in Donaldson, a small community in south-central Arkansas, is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club named for the county it serves. Arkansas has a substantial bowhunting population, and a county-named club like this one often functions as the main organized outlet for local archers rather than one option among several competitors. The ASA tie points to scored 3D archery rounds as part of the club''s regular calendar, practice that tends to matter most in the weeks before deer season opens. Nick Dean is the listed contact for questions about membership, shoot schedules, or course conditions. Further day-to-day details aren''t published beyond that, so reaching out directly is the way to learn more.'),
  ('3b5d919b-5054-4be8-8ae0-933d9b5cdc7f','How ''Bout Dat Archery, based in Oklahoma City, is a USA Archery affiliated club running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program for younger shooters in the metro area. Oklahoma City''s size supports a fairly active archery scene, and a JOAD-affiliated club here gives families access to a structured, Olympic-style recurve curriculum aimed at building fundamentals and, for those interested, a path toward regional or national competition. The club''s distinctive name aside, its core offering centers on that youth development pathway rather than a broader mix of programs. Specific age ranges, practice schedules, and costs for the JOAD program aren''t published, so parents interested in enrolling a young archer should contact the club directly for current details.')
) AS v(id, description)
WHERE r.id = v.id::uuid AND r.is_claimed = false;
